  "live_records": {
    "q-111091": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111091",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-33 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
