    "q-74858": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74858",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
