    },
    "q-111112": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111112",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
