    "q-111154": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111154",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
